  "proofs": [
    "TaskCancel is an explicit additive operation in both immutable task ceiling and invocation grant. It never supplies owner/credential/conversation/task selectors to model arguments. Cancellation invalidates only the bound task grants, leaving sibling task and conversation usable.",
    "Grant revalidation precedes mutation/receipt lookup. Cancellation state, grant revocation, prepared-effect cancellation, journal entry and canonical control receipt commit atomically. Failed receipt writes roll back all changes; current authorized owner can inspect an accepted receipt after grant invalidation.",
    "A real independent MCP client exercises every one of 28 schemas. Invalid selectors/shapes and oversized artifact requests fail without mutation; supported operations have native parity and current authorization.",
    "180-message real MCP recall retrieves an older source omitted from initial bounded context. Pages retain message ID, actor, provenance and state, remain bounded, and deny a sibling task cursor without changing the store.",
    "Abandoned accepted ACK recovers its original receipt and one message. Slow admission and maximum wait return bounded pending handles; late decoded requests return uncertainty retaining task and original mutation IDs. Expired artifact bytes stay inaccessible after replay and reconnect while source references remain retained."
  ],
